(footprint "SW_Kailh_Choc_V1_HotSwap_PTH_6.25u_ChocV1Stab_Diode" (version 20221018) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Kailh Choc V1 (PG1350) low profile mechanical keyboard switch, hot-swap socket, the hole of the socket is plated, single-sided mounting. Plate cut lines: User.1=15.60mm square (cosmetic cover, all switches), User.4=13.80mm square (Kailh Choc V1). Keycap: 6.25u (courtyard 119.01x19.00mm). Kailh Choc 1350 stabilizer: PCB cutout slots (Edge.Cuts) and plate cuts on User.5. Plate required. For Choc V1 switches only (wire interferes with Choc V2). Series diode pads on back side: pad 3 = anode, pad 4 = cathode (cathode bar on B.SilkS, body outline on B.Fab, cathode points left). Combined hand-soldering land for SOD-123 / SOD-323 / MiniMELF (LL-34, LL4148): 2.0x1.4mm pads at +/-1.6mm axial offset. Connect pad 2 to pad 3 (or 1 to 4) externally for the usual row/column matrix.")
  (tags "switch, low_profile, hot_swap, diode")
